  "lifecycle_review": [
    "Same QMP command captures before, synchronously saves a full stream with global_state_store, captures after. No guest register/RAM/IRQ writes added.",
    "O_EXCL refuses overwrite; QIO reference is released after QEMUFile takes it; qemu_fclose runs after save, including save failure. Failed partial streams are not accepted.",
    "Entry capture requires stopped TCG and every VP stopped. Attached BlockBackend storage, network clients and user IOThread objects are rejected.",
    "qmp_query_iothreads only enumerates object_get_objects_root; internal-root IOThreads are not excluded by this guard. Current fixed diskless PC topology only; no general device-quiescence claim.",
    "ram_save_setup releases BQL around multifd synchronization even with multifd disabled. Same-command does not mean BQL continuously held. Observed pre/post and independently restored events match this actual case.",
    "save_snapshot generic migration/replay blockers and block drain are not reproduced by this project helper. It explicitly refuses attached disks and must not be used as a Windows disk checkpoint API."
  ],
  "prior_failures": [
    "compat_restore_v1 lacked identity second2MiB mapping; fixture page fault before target, not a TCG CPU defect.",
    "compat_restore_v2 asynchronous save serialized CPU0 HARD2 although earlier A sampled0; source/target consumer and RAM equality did not waive failed event equality.",
    "v9 build used nonexistent system/bql.h. v10 needed query_iothreads declaration from qapi-commands-misc.h. Those builds were not accepted native sources; final actual source is v11b."
  ],
  "remaining_gates": [
    "Lossless envelope covers all original tcg-state-v1 fields, not all possible x86 MSRs/XSAVE or whole-machine state.",
    "No compatible Unicorn32 loader exists for high hidden bases/extended registers. The new57-name view is not the frozen raw API format.",
    "Actual compatibility-to-long64 microguest is not Windows/WOW64 ABI, kernel resource lifetime or original-game acceptance.",
    "No Windows boot was performed in this reviewed evidence; disks/network/asynchronous devices and active two-VP execution remain unqualified.",
    "RAM SHA comparison uses original observer outputs and fresh restore; this reviewer does not independently decode every compressed migration RAM page.",
    "Original game still requires complete state/ABI/resources, independent replay, tamper rejection and two fresh native lifetimes under unchanged acceptance rules."
  ],
  "native_runs_by_reviewer": 0
}
